# Deliberately NOT `complete:check`. That runs `vite build`, the unit suite AND the full Cypress
# e2e suite — around eight minutes per commit, which is long enough that people reach for
# `--no-verify`, and a hook that gets bypassed protects nothing. CI already runs each of those as
# its own parallel job, so the only thing a commit hook adds is catching what would be
# embarrassing in a diff: a type error, a lint error, unformatted code. Those are seconds.
#
# Before pushing (or opening a PR), run the real gate by hand: `npm run complete:check`.
npm run complete:fast
